From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Collier <jcollier0120@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:29:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] avfilter/vsrc_ddagrab: bind the frames as shader
 resources too

AMF's H.264 encoder and its filters (vpp_amf, sr_amf) convert BGRA
input to NV12 with a compute shader, which needs a shader resource view
of the texture. ddagrab's textures had no D3D11_BIND_SHADER_RESOURCE,
so CreateShaderResourceView() failed with E_INVALIDARG inside AMF, and
h264_amf stopped on the first frame with "SubmitInput() failed with
error 18" (AMF_DIRECTX_FAILED), while hevc_amf and av1_amf, which take
BGRA on the encoder itself, worked. Every format ddagrab captures in
(BGRA, R10G10B10A2, R16G16B16A16_FLOAT) can be bound so, and nothing
else reading the frames changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c b/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c
index e035ac9..1fe09cc 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vsrc_ddagrab.c
@@ -842,6 +842,10 @@ static av_cold int init_hwframes_ctx(AVFilterContext *avctx)
     if (dda->draw_mouse)
         dda->frames_hwctx->BindFlags |= D3D11_BIND_RENDER_TARGET;
 
+    // Readable by shaders too: AMF's H.264 encoder and its filters convert the
+    // frames with a compute shader, and reject a texture without this flag.
+    dda->frames_hwctx->BindFlags |= D3D11_BIND_SHADER_RESOURCE;
+
     ret = av_hwframe_ctx_init(dda->frames_ref);
     if (ret < 0) {
         av_log(avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Failed to initialise hardware frames context: %d.\n", ret);
